      "postID": "646e07e97e46fa488304fea1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In the same way, I'd like you to expose Finger Tracking data as Readonly Animator Parameters too. (I'll create another Canny if needed).\n\nCurrently, SteamVR Input 2.0 allows us to input Finger Tracking data, but it is just as difficult to construct animations based on it as it is when using Eye Tracking.\n\nThe workaround and the problems caused by them are exactly the same, but the number of synced avatar parameters required is very large and the update rate is not fast enough.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-24T12:49:45.304Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With OSC Eye Tracking, we can manipulate the eye tracking by sending values to the address listed [here](https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/osc-eye-tracking#osc-addresses-list).\n\nI don't know whether VRChat uses these internal values for Native Eye Tracking, but we would like to refer these (currently private) values for Animation, as well as parameters such as GestureLeft/Right and Viseme.\n\nIn other words, we would like to drive the Animation **by reading the parameters that would be officially synchronized**.\n\nThis is currently not possible, leaving us with only two options.\n\n- We could do the same thing by sending values to Expression Parameters using OSC, but this require us to use up synced avatar parameters again.\n\n(Remember you once said \"Native eyetracking support will not require you to use up synced avatar parameters,\" in [Developer Update - 2 March 2023](https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-2-march-2023/16706))\n\n- We could put Contacts in the Eye Bone to detect eye movements (only), but this would affect performance and Quest limits.\n\nTherefore, we would like you to expose Native and/or OSC Eye Tracking data as Readonly Animator Parameters.",
